<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="021" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-13: Front Door door — enqueue a run for a submitted request; on Return, release the approved outputs on the request and post a message so the bell fires</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>after:013,010</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api and endpoints; modifies an external-plane endpoint (.cs) shared with another project; external visibility of AI output is a fail-closed concern (FR-13 c).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive external plane: a requester must never see an unapproved output; edits a hot-path file shared with spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4; an open design question (when to enqueue relative to the document upload) needs judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file-overlap with tasks 020 and 022 on the intake DI module and 013's Return-stage hook.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>013, 010</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, endpoints, backend, authorization</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Wire the Front Door into the pipeline: a submitted NDA request (the `POST /api/v1/external/servicerequests` create plus its document upload) gets one run enqueued through task 013's run-submit API, with channel Front Door; on the Return stage for that channel, make the approved outputs visible to the requester on the request and post one message regarding the request through `CommunicationService.PostToRecordThreadAsync` so the requester's bell fires. Coordinate with spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4, which shares these files.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the External Access plane (CIAM callers, record gates), ADR-004 jobs and Dataverse write paths. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Front Door submissions start exactly one run per request (idempotent), a submission without a document lands in manual triage (not a failed run), the requester sees outputs only after approval, and the approval produces one bell-firing message on the request; contract and unit tests cover it.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-13 (a–d), NFR-02, NFR-08. Reuse-scan row 11: extend `SubmitServiceRequestAsync` (ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs:143, create at ~:293) to enqueue a run, and reuse the message path for the return. At authoring time the SPA creates the request first (`intake-client.ts`, `NdaAssessmentWizard.tsx` calls `submitServiceRequest` with no document) and documents go through a separate route, `POST /servicerequests/{id}/documents` (`ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:364`). Enqueuing at create would therefore race the upload; step 1 settles the trigger with the owner. Outputs are persisted on the request by the NDA harness (task 015) and returned only after approval (task 017).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs (SubmitServiceRequestAsync :143, create ~:293)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs (UploadServiceRequestDocument :364) — only if the owner picks the upload trigger</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/FrontDoorReturn.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">the Return-stage hook and intake DI module created by task 013 (exact names set by 013)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpointsTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/FrontDoorReturnTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalMessageEndpoints.cs (PostMessageCoreAsync :210 → CommunicationService.PostToRecordThreadAsync; servicerequests root :84)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs (PostToRecordThreadAsync :2256)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/src/api/intake-client.ts (submit contract) — read only</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">Run-submit API (request id + channel → run, idempotent), Return-stage hook keyed by channel, kill switches.</dependency>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Request channel and current-run columns.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = shared files. `ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs`, `ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs` and the external SPA are shared with spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4: run `/conflict-check` before editing and before the PR; keep the create DTO and its status codes unchanged (no breaking change to `intake-client.ts`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE = the enqueue. Ids only in the payload (request id, run id, correlation id); a deterministic idempotency key per request trigger (e.g. `intake-run:{requestId}:frontdoor`) so a retried submit or upload enqueues one run.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">SCOPE = the Front Door door. A door kill switch (`Intake:Doors:FrontDoor:Enabled`) makes the enqueue a no-op; the existing create and upload behave exactly as before.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">SCOPE = the external routes touched. Their existing filters, CIAM checks and record gates stay unchanged; no new external route is added.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">SCOPE = output visibility. An output document is reachable by the requester only after the run is Approved: release happens in `FrontDoorReturn` (the approved version from 017), never at Persist. Fail closed: if release cannot be confirmed, nothing is released and the run is held with admin attention.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">SCOPE = the return message. Post through `CommunicationService.PostToRecordThreadAsync` regarding the request, app-only; one message per run (marker before post, key `intake-return-msg:{runId}`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = message text and logs. Fixed text ("Your request has been reviewed; the documents are on the request") plus the request number; no document or clause text; logs carry ids only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = test data. Synthetic NDAs only; never real NDAs or the accelerator `answer-key/` (NFR-10).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE = this task's BFF changes. State the Placement Justification in the PR (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (total ≤ 60 MB); no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-004-job-contract.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
