      <file>docs/architecture/external-access-spa-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_servicerequest.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>tests/CLAUDE.md (new tests go under KEEP paths: contract/auth/data-mutation)</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Endpoint filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Existing external filters stay in place.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Endpoint definition" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md">No new route; ProblemDetails unchanged.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Access control" location=".claude/patterns/auth/uac-access-control.md">External visibility of documents.</pattern>
      <pattern name="SSO binding" location=".claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md">Caller principal on external routes.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load the knowledge files; trace the Front Door NDA flow (wizard → create → document upload) and how a `sprk_document` on a request becomes visible to the requester; declare RIGOR FULL, tier opus, effort high. Then fire the first escalation trigger with the options before coding.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the owner-chosen trigger: call 013's run-submit API with channel Front Door after the create (and/or upload) succeeds; the enqueue never changes the HTTP response of the existing route; enqueue failure is logged and leaves the request for admin re-drive (task 023), never a 500 to the requester.</step>
    <step order="3">Ensure Persist (015) leaves outputs invisible to the requester; implement `FrontDoorReturn` (registered on 013's Return hook for channel Front Door): release the approved versions to the requester, then post the one message.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: contract tests on the create/upload route (one run per request, kill switch off → no enqueue, unchanged status codes) and unit tests on `FrontDoorReturn` (release then message, marker, hold on failure).</step>
    <step order="5">Build and run tests; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record the trigger decision and the r4 coordination in projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Before coding, STOP and ask the owner (root CLAUDE.md §6) which event enqueues the run, because the create and the document upload are separate calls: (A) on the first document upload to an NDA-type request, recommended, no DTO change; (B) the SPA calls a new "submit complete" route after upload (SPA + new route, coordinate with r4); (C) the create accepts the document in one multipart call (breaking change to the r4-owned contract). Also confirm FR-13(d): with (A), who enqueues the triage run for a request that never gets a document.</trigger>
    <trigger>If outputs persisted by task 015 are already visible to the requester before approval, STOP and escalate (FR-13 c, security) rather than patching visibility in this task.</trigger>
    <trigger>If spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4 has open changes to the same functions, STOP and coordinate before editing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row 11: `ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs:110` (`SubmitServiceRequestAsync` :143) is extended; `ExternalMessageEndpoints.cs` / `CommunicationService.PostToRecordThreadAsync` is reused for the return message. CAPABILITY-INDEX row 12 (communication send/post).</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the door (the submit route is extended, not replaced). `FrontDoorReturn` is new only because the Return stage needs a per-channel step (release + message) that no existing component performs.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A Front Door NDA submission never becomes a run, and an approved review never reaches the requester or rings their bell, so FR-13 and success criterion 4 fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">Shared-file check with r4</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/FrontDoorReturn.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpointsTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/FrontDoorReturnTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A Front Door NDA submission (with its document, per the chosen trigger) enqueues exactly one run with channel Front Door; a retried call enqueues no second run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A submission with no document creates the request and reaches the manual-triage path, not a Failed run (FR-13 d).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing create route's DTO, status codes and error codes are unchanged (existing contract tests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the Front Door kill switch off, no run is enqueued and the create/upload behave as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: before approval the requester cannot list or open any output document of the run (FR-13 c); a release failure releases nothing and holds the run with admin attention.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On Return, the approved versions become visible to the requester and exactly one message is posted regarding the request; a redelivered Return posts no second message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No log or message contains document or clause text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build and all tests pass; the PR states the Placement Justification, the publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE) and the r4 coordination. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. One seeding proof for the "no output visible before approval" guard.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>FR-13(a) and (b) are verified live on dev in task 029. The SPA's NDA wizard has no document upload at authoring time; if the chosen trigger needs SPA work, that work is coordinated with r4 and may become its own task. External SPA build note (memory): the BFF host is baked in at Vite build time.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute (FULL rigor).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
